('advanced-native-1898', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1898-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["數碼媒體是成長重要部分，其他人際影響也仍在。"],"options":["他們只用裝置收看故事，不透過它跟朋友談話。","數碼媒體是成長重要部分，其他人際影響也仍在。","他們只到成年後才偶爾用過一次裝置。","家庭和老師已被敘述為完全沒有任何影響。"]},"advanced-native-1898-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["We grew up on screens, though family and teachers remained important influences too.","Devices were an ordinary way for us to follow stories and keep up with friends.","Digital experiences formed part of our daily life rather than a single isolated event.","We experienced media alongside conversations that helped us question it."],"options":["We grew up on screens, though family and teachers remained important influences too.","Devices were an ordinary way for us to follow stories and keep up with friends.","Digital experiences formed part of our daily life rather than a single isolated event.","We experienced media alongside conversations that helped us question it."]},"advanced-native-1898-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Beginning regular tablet use in adulthood does not establish that he grew up on screens."],"options":["Regular use now establishes that the device was a major part of his childhood.","The account is about parents choosing childhood media routines, rather than his adult workplace learning.","Beginning regular tablet use in adulthood does not establish that he grew up on screens."]},"advanced-native-1898-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["父母、老師和面對面關係都沒有參與影響。"],"options":["仍可具體說使用哪些媒體及怎樣接觸。","數碼媒體在成長日常有重要位置。","父母、老師和面對面關係都沒有參與影響。"]},"advanced-native-1898-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We grew up on screens, but that describes one major part of the experience, not the absence of family influence."],"options":["We grew up on screens, but that describes one major part of the experience, not the absence of family influence.","I had read “on screens” as excluding those family conversations.","I would describe the media only by the devices we owned, without discussing how we used them."]},"advanced-native-1898-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Before saying that he and his whole generation grew up on screens, could we ask him what place the tablet actually had in his childhood? The photograph shows one moment, not the absence of family or face-to-face life.","I would use an interview, not this photograph alone, to explore whether he grew up on screens and what that meant in his daily life. His own memories could make the caption more accurate without claiming to speak for a generation."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1899', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1899-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["傳聞傳得快，但實際安排仍待主辦者查核。"],"options":["傳聞仍停在私人草稿，尚未傳進群組。","這個速度形容已提供傳聞內容真確的證據。","傳聞傳得快，但實際安排仍待主辦者查核。","主辦者已確認取消，所有訊息只是轉發正式通知。"]},"advanced-native-1899-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["People were passing on the cancellation claim while the organiser was still checking it.","The message travelled faster than the confirmation process.","The discussion had moved ahead of what the organiser actually knew about the room.","The rumour spread at the speed of light through the chat before the arrangement was confirmed."],"options":["People were passing on the cancellation claim while the organiser was still checking it.","The message travelled faster than the confirmation process.","The discussion had moved ahead of what the organiser actually knew about the room.","The rumour spread at the speed of light through the chat before the arrangement was confirmed."]},"advanced-native-1899-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["News can spread at the speed of light after being checked; here the account explicitly puts the official check before the forwarding."],"options":["The rapid circulation is evidence that the student skipped the official announcement.","The account says the official check happened only after the summary had already been forwarded.","News can spread at the speed of light after being checked; here the account explicitly puts the official check before the forwarding."]},"advanced-native-1899-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["內容因此已獲查證是真確。"],"options":["內容因此已獲查證是真確。","仍需其他資料知道實際速度與範圍。","說話者誇張地形容傳得很快。"]},"advanced-native-1899-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["It spread at the speed of light, but that tells us about circulation, not verification; let’s check the organiser’s update."],"options":["It spread at the speed of light, but that tells us about circulation, not verification; let’s check the organiser’s update.","I thought the number of quick forwards was enough to show the booking had been checked.","I would use the first forwarded message as the final answer before looking at the organiser’s account."]},"advanced-native-1899-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The recipe-story appeal has travelled at the speed of light, and thank you for the replies already arriving. Could you send further contributions to the shared inbox so we can organise them and confirm the names to use?","News of the family collection spread at the speed of light beyond the first group. We appreciate the interest; please use the shared address for new stories rather than leave them across several chats."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1901', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1901-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["作者用葉子描寫外顯喜好，並把它跟較深根基作比喻對比。"],"options":["這份敘述已查證每個人的家庭與媒體影響都有同樣分工。","作者把網上材料放在深層根基，把風格喜好交給其他經驗。","作者用葉子描寫外顯喜好，並把它跟較深根基作比喻對比。","作者只說互聯網改變最深價值，沒有用葉子指品味。"]},"advanced-native-1901-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It is linked with the more outward preferences, rather than described only as a deeper foundation.","The writer associates it with changing tastes in the visible part of the imagined tree.","Its role is illustrated through style and preference, within one interpretation of different influences.","It colours the leaves by shaping visible styles and tastes in the tree comparison."],"options":["It is linked with the more outward preferences, rather than described only as a deeper foundation.","The writer associates it with changing tastes in the visible part of the imagined tree.","Its role is illustrated through style and preference, within one interpretation of different influences.","It colours the leaves by shaping visible styles and tastes in the tree comparison."]},"advanced-native-1901-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Saying the internet only colours the leaves may understate this account, which describes a deeper reconsideration of responsibility."],"options":["The tree image already establishes that online material cannot affect a career decision.","Saying the internet only colours the leaves may understate this account, which describes a deeper reconsideration of responsibility.","The account describes only a change of clothing taste, with no reconsideration of responsibility."]},"advanced-native-1901-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["已證明媒體只能影響表面，永遠不能觸及價值。"],"options":["已證明媒體只能影響表面，永遠不能觸及價值。","可以再問這個圖像是否涵蓋人物所有經驗。","作者把某些可見喜好比作葉子。"]},"advanced-native-1901-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The internet colours the leaves in that image, but I would still compare it with what the person actually says changed."],"options":["I thought naming the roots and leaves already told us which experiences must be superficial.","I would choose the image first and fit the interview into its two categories afterwards.","The internet colours the leaves in that image, but I would still compare it with what the person actually says changed."]},"advanced-native-1901-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["In this year’s album, the internet colours the leaves through the clothes and music I tried with online friends. My monthly cooking with Gran remains important to me; this is my account of the year, not a rule about everyone’s influences.","The internet colours the leaves of my year in these changing styles, while the meals with Gran reflect an enduring commitment. I like the image for this album, without assuming it describes every online experience I might have."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1903', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1903-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["說話者受到吸引，同時仍保留選擇與舊喜好。"],"options":["說話者受到吸引，同時仍保留選擇與舊喜好。","說話者已只聽新風格，不再保留舊喜好。","朋友沒有介紹任何新風格，只要求大家聽相同舊歌。","說話者先決定採納整套風格，之後才首次聽朋友介紹。"]},"advanced-native-1903-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["I took some ideas from it without treating the whole trend as a requirement.","I felt the pull of modern influence, but chose what interested me rather than replacing all my favourites.","I was curious about what my friends shared while still enjoying older songs.","The trend drew my attention, but did not make every choice for me."],"options":["I took some ideas from it without treating the whole trend as a requirement.","I felt the pull of modern influence, but chose what interested me rather than replacing all my favourites.","I was curious about what my friends shared while still enjoying older songs.","The trend drew my attention, but did not make every choice for me."]},"advanced-native-1903-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The pull of modern influence can be present without the person adopting the trend; her stated choice still matters."],"options":["Her decision to keep the earlier practice is described as having been made before she heard about the trend.","The pull of modern influence can be present without the person adopting the trend; her stated choice still matters.","A trend’s attraction establishes that she has already replaced her earlier practice."]},"advanced-native-1903-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["接觸到風潮的人一定已照它改變選擇。"],"options":["仍需人物實際反應才知道影響程度。","當代風潮可能吸引或牽引人。","接觸到風潮的人一定已照它改變選擇。"]},"advanced-native-1903-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["I can feel the pull of modern influence and still choose only some elements; influence is not the same as copying the whole trend."],"options":["I thought keeping an older favourite meant none of the new style could have interested me.","I thought finding the trend attractive meant I had already adopted it, even before trying any part of it.","I can feel the pull of modern influence and still choose only some elements; influence is not the same as copying the whole trend."]},"advanced-native-1903-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["I can see the pull of modern influence in the room design, but our current taste is not evidence of what people in that period preferred. Could we check the period accounts before deciding which details are historical and which are our interpretation?","The pull of modern influence may explain why we like that style, not why the character would have chosen it. Let’s separate the documented details from our present-day additions in the design notes."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1904', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1904-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["人物把精選展示當成評價自己生活的框架。"],"options":["朋友已停止看動態，這段只報告刪除帳戶的步驟。","人物把精選展示當成評價自己生活的框架。","人物只用帳戶查活動時間，沒有比較自己。","敘述者把精選動態當作朋友周末的完整客觀記錄。"]},"advanced-native-1904-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It becomes the mirror through which young people see themselves as they compare their own weekends with selected images.","It supplies a frame against which the friends judge their ordinary lives.","The characters begin treating the display as a standard for how they see themselves.","Its effect in this account concerns self-evaluation, not only finding information online."],"options":["It becomes the mirror through which young people see themselves as they compare their own weekends with selected images.","It supplies a frame against which the friends judge their ordinary lives.","The characters begin treating the display as a standard for how they see themselves.","Its effect in this account concerns self-evaluation, not only finding information online."]},"advanced-native-1904-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["This use alone does not show that the feed has become the mirror through which young people see themselves; the account gives no self-evaluation through it."],"options":["This use alone does not show that the feed has become the mirror through which young people see themselves; the account gives no self-evaluation through it.","The account already describes her comparing her appearance with selected images in the feed.","The account describes her comparing personal achievements, rather than looking for travel information."]},"advanced-native-1904-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["已知每個年輕人都以同樣方式理解自己。"],"options":["已知每個年輕人都以同樣方式理解自己。","仍應看個別人物怎樣比較與反應。","人物可能藉媒體框架評價自己。"]},"advanced-native-1904-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["It is the mirror through which young people see themselves in this account because the characters use those images to judge their own weekends."],"options":["I thought selected images could only supply information about others, never a frame for self-comparison.","I would treat the feed as a complete record of everyone’s weekends before asking how the images were selected.","It is the mirror through which young people see themselves in this account because the characters use those images to judge their own weekends."]},"advanced-native-1904-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The feed may become the mirror through which young people see themselves, but we should not use her selected achievements as her whole identity. Could the profile also include what she says about practice and ordinary days?","If we discuss the mirror through which young people see themselves, let’s include her explanation of what she leaves out of the feed. That would make the profile more than a copy of the public images."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1905', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1905-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["家庭習慣參與形成核心價值，之後仍有其他經驗影響。"],"options":["她成年合作時才首次提出承認錯誤，家中沒有出現這種例子。","其他經驗已被排除，不再影響她如何合作。","家庭習慣參與形成核心價值，之後仍有其他經驗影響。","她只學到一種報告格式，沒有提價值形成。"]},"advanced-native-1905-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It contributed a principle she later brought into group work.","The example at home helped her value admitting an error rather than concealing it.","It was one source of a central value, while later experiences affected how she used it.","It helped shape the backbone of her outlook by making honesty about mistakes important."],"options":["It contributed a principle she later brought into group work.","The example at home helped her value admitting an error rather than concealing it.","It was one source of a central value, while later experiences affected how she used it.","It helped shape the backbone of her outlook by making honesty about mistakes important."]},"advanced-native-1905-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["A colour preference alone does not establish an influence that shapes the backbone of her outlook."],"options":["A colour preference alone does not establish an influence that shapes the backbone of her outlook.","The account identifies a fairness principle that she continues using when making decisions.","Her temporary choice of a fashionable colour is enough to identify the principle guiding her later decisions."]},"advanced-native-1905-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["之後任何經驗都不能再改變她的應用方式。"],"options":["參與塑造支撐觀點的核心價值。","之後任何經驗都不能再改變她的應用方式。","可用具體榜樣與後來做法說明作用。"]},"advanced-native-1905-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["They helped shape the backbone of my outlook, but I still need to think about how those principles apply in a different situation."],"options":["They helped shape the backbone of my outlook, but I still need to think about how those principles apply in a different situation.","I thought keeping a principle meant repeating the same action without checking the circumstances.","I thought questioning how to apply the principle now meant it had never influenced me in the first place."]},"advanced-native-1905-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The rule about never contradicting elders helped shape the backbone of my outlook, which is why speaking up felt disloyal. I now want to learn how to disagree respectfully when staying quiet would leave someone treated unfairly.","Those early rules shaped the backbone of my outlook, but I am beginning to question whether politeness must mean agreement. Could I talk with you about a respectful way to challenge the arrangement affecting our classmate?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1907', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1907-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["團隊面對可能失去榮譽的壓力，仍承認需要更正。"],"options":["團隊面對可能失去榮譽的壓力，仍承認需要更正。","團隊只在獲保證不會失去任何榮譽後，才承認貢獻。","團隊雖承認有人幫忙，仍拒絕承認原本漏了署名。","團隊堅持保留錯誤署名，理由是自己一向重視誠實。"]},"advanced-native-1907-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The choice was supported by a principle about honest credit, not only a claim to be honest.","It showed moral backbone by admitting the uncredited contribution despite the possible cost to its recognition.","The members corrected their public account rather than let the award hide the missing credit.","They accepted a difficult consequence in order to acknowledge someone else’s work."],"options":["The choice was supported by a principle about honest credit, not only a claim to be honest.","It showed moral backbone by admitting the uncredited contribution despite the possible cost to its recognition.","The members corrected their public account rather than let the award hide the missing credit.","They accepted a difficult consequence in order to acknowledge someone else’s work."]},"advanced-native-1907-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Refusing to correct a disproved claim is not by itself moral backbone; ethical firmness can require acknowledging new evidence."],"options":["Her explanation identifies new evidence that supports the original accusation.","The account describes her checking the new material before giving reasons for keeping the accusation.","Refusing to correct a disproved claim is not by itself moral backbone; ethical firmness can require acknowledging new evidence."]},"advanced-native-1907-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["只要從不改口，就必定行事正當。"],"options":["只要從不改口，就必定行事正當。","仍需要具體選擇與理由支持評價。","可指有壓力仍守住道德原則。"]},"advanced-native-1907-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Moral backbone can mean correcting our own account when the evidence requires it, even if keeping the award would be easier."],"options":["I thought standing by a principle meant keeping the original account regardless of a missing contribution.","I would judge the choice only by whether the team keeps its recognition, not by how it handles the credit.","Moral backbone can mean correcting our own account when the evidence requires it, even if keeping the award would be easier."]},"advanced-native-1907-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Her moral backbone appears in refusing to report agreement that has not been given, not in opposing the group for its own sake. She can still contact the absent classmate rather than treat the deadline as permission to invent consent.","The captain shows moral backbone when she keeps the form accurate under pressure to finish. Asking the classmate directly would continue that principle while giving the group a practical next step."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1909', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1909-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["親身經驗讓說話者較願意重新理解同一建議。"],"options":["導師已換了一套相反建議，說話者沒有重聽原來內容。","說話者只在核對錄音音量，沒有提理解角度。","親身經驗讓說話者較願意重新理解同一建議。","說話者第一次解釋時已提出現在的全部問題。"]},"advanced-native-1909-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The attempt gave me an experience to connect with the explanation.","I was ready to notice details I had not recognised as important before.","The same advice met a different stage of my understanding.","I heard it with fresher ears after trying the task and developing more specific questions."],"options":["The attempt gave me an experience to connect with the explanation.","I was ready to notice details I had not recognised as important before.","The same advice met a different stage of my understanding.","I heard it with fresher ears after trying the task and developing more specific questions."]},"advanced-native-1909-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The same recording can be heard with fresher ears when later experience changes the listener’s questions."],"options":["The same recording can be heard with fresher ears when later experience changes the listener’s questions.","An unchanged recording establishes that the listener must bring exactly the same understanding each time.","The account says the interviewer replaced the answer, rather than the listener bringing new experience."]},"advanced-native-1909-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["新的解讀因此必定沒有錯漏。"],"options":["新的解讀因此必定沒有錯漏。","仍可比較新舊理解及核對內容。","聆聽角度比先前有更新。"]},"advanced-native-1909-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["I can hear it with fresher ears now that I have tried the task; I want to check the parts I did not know to question before."],"options":["I thought being more open to the recording now meant my new interpretation needed no further checking.","I can hear it with fresher ears now that I have tried the task; I want to check the parts I did not know to question before.","I thought a repeat listening could matter only if the speaker had changed the words."]},"advanced-native-1909-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Could we return to the poem with fresher ears tomorrow, choosing one line each before we discuss it again? I would like us to explain what we actually hear in the words rather than immediately search for a single approved answer.","Let’s read it with fresher ears after a short pause and bring a line we want to try aloud. We can compare our reasons without treating the break as proof that either interpretation must be right."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1910', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1910-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["競爭壓力可能使人偏離已認同的準確性要求。"],"options":["這句已證明每位成員都取消了檢查並交稿。","故事只說伙伴有不同喜好，沒有交代報告目標。","競爭壓力可能使人偏離已認同的準確性要求。","團隊正在提醒彼此完成檢查，沒有略過的壓力。"]},"advanced-native-1910-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Finishing first was beginning to compete with the report’s accuracy goal.","The risk was a shortcut that undermined their own agreed standard.","The concern is that keeping pace with the group could make us drop the accuracy checks we agreed to carry out.","It could pull people in the wrong direction by making them skip checks they had agreed were important."],"options":["Finishing first was beginning to compete with the report’s accuracy goal.","The risk was a shortcut that undermined their own agreed standard.","The concern is that keeping pace with the group could make us drop the accuracy checks we agreed to carry out.","It could pull people in the wrong direction by making them skip checks they had agreed were important."]},"advanced-native-1910-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Peer influence alone does not establish pressure that pulls people in the wrong direction; here the encouragement supports the agreed accuracy goal."],"options":["The student has already completed the check, and the account is reviewing the result.","Peer influence alone does not establish pressure that pulls people in the wrong direction; here the encouragement supports the agreed accuracy goal.","The encouragement is mainly to finish ahead of others, rather than carry out the agreed checking first."]},"advanced-native-1910-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["所有朋友的建議都必須視為有害。"],"options":["應有理由說明甚麼目標或原則正被偏離。","某種影響可能令人偏向不合適選擇。","所有朋友的建議都必須視為有害。"]},"advanced-native-1910-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["That pressure can pull people in the wrong direction if fitting in means dropping the checks we agreed to do. Could we keep the standard and discuss the deadline instead?"],"options":["I thought matching the other members’ pace was enough to show the checking had been done.","I would compare only who finishes first, not whether the report meets the standard we set.","That pressure can pull people in the wrong direction if fitting in means dropping the checks we agreed to do. Could we keep the standard and discuss the deadline instead?"]},"advanced-native-1910-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Wanting to agree with familiar friends can pull people in the wrong direction when we assume the new member does not need a say. Could we ask him before deciding how to handle the refund?","This is the kind of pressure that can pull people in the wrong direction: we are treating silence as agreement without asking. I would include the new member in the refund discussion rather than decide what he should feel."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1911', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1911-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["她用建築描寫家校角色，也承認其他人的影響。"],"options":["家長提供根基後，教師被描述為毋須再用日常例子。","她用建築描寫家校角色，也承認其他人的影響。","她把培育看成只在家完成，老師只負責評分。","她認為老師應取代家庭，其他照顧者不參與。"]},"advanced-native-1911-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["In her image, parents lay the foundation; teachers strengthen the structure through everyday examples.","Parents provide an early basis, and teachers help develop it through practice.","The two roles contribute to development rather than one automatically completing the work alone.","She uses a building comparison while leaving room for friends and other carers as well."],"options":["In her image, parents lay the foundation; teachers strengthen the structure through everyday examples.","Parents provide an early basis, and teachers help develop it through practice.","The two roles contribute to development rather than one automatically completing the work alone.","She uses a building comparison while leaving room for friends and other carers as well."]},"advanced-native-1911-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The image “parents lay the foundation; teachers strengthen the structure” should not replace the different roles this person actually describes."],"options":["The building image establishes that the grandmother’s role can be omitted from this person’s account.","The account already identifies the same parental and teacher roles as the summary uses.","The image “parents lay the foundation; teachers strengthen the structure” should not replace the different roles this person actually describes."]},"advanced-native-1911-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["每個孩子都只能受這兩方影響，其他經驗不算。"],"options":["仍應說日常例子怎支持原則。","兩方可分別提供早期基礎及持續鞏固。","每個孩子都只能受這兩方影響，其他經驗不算。"]},"advanced-native-1911-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["“Parents lay the foundation; teachers strengthen the structure” is a useful image only if we can show what those roles involve in daily practice."],"options":["I thought