e interest meant I should also adopt the same place and timing for every major decision."]},"advanced-native-1918-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["This interview offers ideas about a writing practice, not an invitation to copy someone else’s life line by line. Notice what helped her work, then ask what might need to change in your own circumstances.","We do not need to copy someone else’s life line by line to learn from this account. Her timetable belongs to her conditions; the useful question is which habits we can adapt, not whether our days can look identical."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
