('advanced-native-1934', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1934-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["批評的是評價過窄，想把新會員的學習進展也納入。"],"options":["批評的是評價過窄，想把新會員的學習進展也納入。","委員會從未記錄任何比賽結果。","新會員已被要求只談進步，不可再參賽。","學會已決定比賽勝仗足以代表全部學習。"]},"advanced-native-1934-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The concern was not having goals, but failing to consider progress beyond prizes.","It was too results-driven because the review counted wins while overlooking what newcomers learned.","The committee used a narrow measure and left out the beginners’ development.","Competition totals had become the main answer to a question about learning."],"options":["The concern was not having goals, but failing to consider progress beyond prizes.","It was too results-driven because the review counted wins while overlooking what newcomers learned.","The committee used a narrow measure and left out the beginners’ development.","Competition totals had become the main answer to a question about learning."]},"advanced-native-1934-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Being results-driven does not establish that this team ignores the process; the account includes quality and experience checks."],"options":["Being results-driven does not establish that this team ignores the process; the account includes quality and experience checks.","The team’s stated targets show that it excluded all feedback on how the work was done.","The account says only the number of completed tasks was reviewed."]},"advanced-native-1934-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["too 明確批評程度過高；基本形容詞本身可中性描述導向。"],"options":["兩者都必定指已取得優秀成果。","too 明確批評程度過高；基本形容詞本身可中性描述導向。","只要用基本形容詞，就表示團隊沒有任何目標。"]},"advanced-native-1934-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We can be results-driven without counting prizes alone; let’s include the learning we actually want the club to support."],"options":["I thought questioning the prize total meant we should stop asking what the club achieves.","I would keep the same prize measure and add more categories of competition wins.","We can be results-driven without counting prizes alone; let’s include the learning we actually want the club to support."]},"advanced-native-1934-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["I am interested in your results-driven team; could you describe one service goal and how you judge whether it helps the people using it? Before I decide to join, I would also like to know whom a new member can ask when the work is unclear.","What does results-driven mean in your everyday work, and could you give an example of an outcome you aim for? I would like to understand both the goal and the support available to newcomers before making a commitment."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1935', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1935-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["課堂同時提供資料，並培養比較敘述和證據的判斷。"],"options":["課堂認為事實全無用途，只看學生喜好。","學生只抄下日期，沒有比較任何敘述。","老師已要求所有學生接受同一份敘述而不看證據。","課堂同時提供資料，並培養比較敘述和證據的判斷。"]},"advanced-native-1935-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It adds practice in evaluating accounts rather than only recalling information.","The facts become material for reasoned comparison, not just a list to remember.","It shows how education does not simply fill the mind, because pupils compare accounts and the evidence behind them.","Students learn to ask why descriptions of the same event differ."],"options":["It adds practice in evaluating accounts rather than only recalling information.","The facts become material for reasoned comparison, not just a list to remember.","It shows how education does not simply fill the mind, because pupils compare accounts and the evidence behind them.","Students learn to ask why descriptions of the same event differ."]},"advanced-native-1935-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The list may add knowledge, but this account does not yet show how education does not simply fill the mind."],"options":["The list may add knowledge, but this account does not yet show how education does not simply fill the mind.","The account already describes students comparing explanations of the dates.","The activity asks pupils to apply the chronology to a new historical question."]},"advanced-native-1935-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["教育不應提供任何事實或知識。"],"options":["教育不應提供任何事實或知識。","可再說明有哪些比較或應用活動。","教育可包括知識以外的理解發展。"]},"advanced-native-1935-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Education does not simply fill the mind, but reliable facts can give us something to question, compare and use."],"options":["I would add a longer fact list instead of an opportunity to use the facts.","Education does not simply fill the mind, but reliable facts can give us something to question, compare and use.","I thought developing judgement meant we should ask students to decide without examining any information."]},"advanced-native-1935-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Education does not simply fill the mind, so could our cards ask visitors to use one visible detail to suggest an object’s purpose? They could then compare the suggestion with the label and explain what they would revise.","To show how education does not simply fill the mind, I suggest adding a question about one object rather than only naming it. Visitors can support an initial idea with a detail, then check the label before treating that idea as established."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1937', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1937-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["後來初稿可見講評的影響，但不是唯一來源。"],"options":["敘述只說講評時間改了，沒有談初稿做法。","後來初稿可見講評的影響，但不是唯一來源。","導師已把所有改變只歸於講評，排除閱讀。","小組仍只列細節，從不解釋選取理由。"]},"advanced-native-1937-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The critique leaves a clear fingerprint in the way members explain their choice of details.","Their new habit of giving reasons reflects something practised in the weekly sessions.","The work carries a recognisable trace of the feedback discussions.","I can connect that part of the drafting practice with the critique, without claiming it is the only source."],"options":["The critique leaves a clear fingerprint in the way members explain their choice of details.","Their new habit of giving reasons reflects something practised in the weekly sessions.","The work carries a recognisable trace of the feedback discussions.","I can connect that part of the drafting practice with the critique, without claiming it is the only source."]},"advanced-native-1937-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["A shared feature alone does not establish that one writer left a clear fingerprint on the other’s work."],"options":["A shared feature alone does not establish that one writer left a clear fingerprint on the other’s work.","The account already documents one writer studying the other’s drafts.","The shared short sentences identify the direction of influence without further context."]},"advanced-native-1937-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["相似特徵本身已排除其他影響來源。"],"options":["可說明哪些細節及背景支持影響判斷。","作品可見某種獨特影響。","相似特徵本身已排除其他影響來源。"]},"advanced-native-1937-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Before saying one writer left a clear fingerprint on another’s work, could we check the reading history as well as the resemblance?"],"options":["I thought matching sentence lengths already told us which writer had learnt from the other.","I would compare only the finished paragraphs, without asking when either writer first saw the work.","Before saying one writer left a clear fingerprint on another’s work, could we check the reading history as well as the resemblance?"]},"advanced-native-1937-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The workshop seems to have left a clear fingerprint on the layered paper, while the colours and local story are your later choices. Could you tell me which techniques to acknowledge and how you would like that training credited on the label?","Before writing that the training left a clear fingerprint on this piece, I would like to distinguish what you learnt there from what you developed afterwards. Which features should the label connect with the workshop, and what wording would you prefer for the credit?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1938', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1938-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["共同詞彙讓討論較可行，但未令大家已同意方案。"],"options":["共同詞彙讓討論較可行，但未令大家已同意方案。","成員已一致選好版本，沒有留下分歧。","小組還沒有任何共用名稱，只在分配座位。","共同詞彙取消了比較不同版本的需要。"]},"advanced-native-1938-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It prepared a more precise conversation rather than deciding the design.","It set the stage for detailed discussion by helping us identify the same parts.","We could explain differences without first guessing which part someone meant.","The terms gave us a basis for comparing versions, even though we still disagreed."],"options":["It prepared a more precise conversation rather than deciding the design.","It set the stage for detailed discussion by helping us identify the same parts.","We could explain differences without first guessing which part someone meant.","The terms gave us a basis for comparing versions, even though we still disagreed."]},"advanced-native-1938-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The exchange may set the stage for an agreement, but the account does not report an agreement yet."],"options":["The exchange may set the stage for an agreement, but the account does not report an agreement yet.","The account says both sides have already approved the same proposal.","Providing available times is described as a completed decision about the proposal itself."]},"advanced-native-1938-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["討論已完成，並達成同意。"],"options":["為討論準備條件。","討論已完成，並達成同意。","可說明哪些資訊讓討論較可行。"]},"advanced-native-1938-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["That may set the stage for agreement, but we should describe the meeting as a next step rather than announce a result we do not have."],"options":["That may set the stage for agreement, but we should describe the meeting as a next step rather than announce a result we do not have.","I thought being willing to meet meant both sides had already accepted the same terms.","I would schedule the public announcement before asking what either side wants to discuss."]},"advanced-native-1938-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["A choice of what to share could set the stage for trust without asking for a personal story at the first meeting. Could we invite one object people are willing to discuss and make listening an equal option?","To set the stage for later conversation, I suggest an optional object-sharing activity, with no requirement to explain private experiences. We can invite participation without claiming everyone already feels close."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1939', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1939-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["學校有作用，家庭責任也影響選擇，並非單一來源決定全部。"],"options":["敘述否認老師曾給她任何鼓勵。","學校已決定她必須接受每個機會。","照顧弟弟被寫成她在接受全部演出機會後，才開始的責任。","學校有作用，家庭責任也影響選擇，並非單一來源決定全部。"]},"advanced-native-1939-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["She is showing another influence rather than denying what the teacher contributed.","Her account connects education with the other conditions of her life.","School does not write every line of the script; her opportunities were also shaped by responsibilities at home.","The teacher’s encouragement was important, but did not explain every choice available to her."],"options":["She is showing another influence rather than denying what the teacher contributed.","Her account connects education with the other conditions of her life.","School does not write every line of the script; her opportunities were also shaped by responsibilities at home.","The teacher’s encouragement was important, but did not explain every choice available to her."]},"advanced-native-1939-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Saying school does not write every line of the script leaves room for its influence alongside later experiences."],"options":["Saying school does not write every line of the script leaves room for its influence alongside later experiences.","The account reports that no school experience influenced his thinking.","The later changes are described as proof that the school influence never existed."]},"advanced-native-1939-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["那種來源沒有產生任何影響。"],"options":["那種來源沒有產生任何影響。","仍可討論其他條件與後來選擇。","某種來源不是全部發展的唯一決定者。"]},"advanced-native-1939-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["School does not write every line of the script, but I can still thank the teacher for the encouragement she gave me."],"options":["School does not write every line of the script, but I can still thank the teacher for the encouragement she gave me.","I thought recognising another influence meant the teacher’s contribution no longer counted.","I would explain the whole choice through school alone because that makes a simpler thank-you."]},"advanced-native-1939-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The childhood criticism does not write every line of the script; the later friendships also change what she is willing to attempt. Our introduction could invite readers to trace those encounters rather than explain the ending through one early scene alone.","Her early experience matters, but it does not write every line of the script in this novel. I would ask how the friends’ different responses affect her next choices, without treating any one encounter as the complete cause."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1940', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1940-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["課程有貢獻，鄰里及工作經驗也參與轉變。"],"options":["鄰居只是課堂的虛構角色，沒有實際接觸。","課程有貢獻，鄰里及工作經驗也參與轉變。","課程被描述為全部轉變的唯一來源。","說話者否認課程提供任何練習。"]},"advanced-native-1940-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It was one thread in a much larger fabric, alongside work and contact with neighbours.","The course gave me practice, but other experiences also shaped how I communicated.","I see it as a contribution to the change rather than the complete cause.","Its effect belongs in an account that also includes the people I met outside class."],"options":["It was one thread in a much larger fabric, alongside work and contact with neighbours.","The course gave me practice, but other experiences also shaped how I communicated.","I see it as a contribution to the change rather than the complete cause.","Its effect belongs in an account that also includes the people I met outside class."]},"advanced-native-1940-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Family experience is one thread in a much larger fabric here; the account also names work and reading."],"options":["The person identifies family as the only source of the change.","The account says work and reading had no connection with the new routine.","Family experience is one thread in a much larger fabric here; the account also names work and reading."]},"advanced-native-1940-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["因為不是全部，所以沒有重要作用。"],"options":["它是整體中的一項貢獻。","因為不是全部，所以沒有重要作用。","可以再問其他因素怎樣互相連結。"]},"advanced-native-1940-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["It is one thread in a much larger fabric, but the practice it provided still belongs in the account."],"options":["It is one thread in a much larger fabric, but the practice it provided still belongs in the account.","I thought an influence was worth mentioning only if it explained the whole change.","I would turn the course into the single cause so the introduction has a simpler structure."]},"advanced-native-1940-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The painter’s skill is one thread in a much larger fabric of work that includes the residents’ stories and the students’ careful editing. Let us thank each group for the part it actually contributed to this mural.","The painter’s contribution is one thread in a much larger fabric, alongside the residents’ stories and the students’ editing. Thank you to each group for bringing these different kinds of work into one mural."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1941', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1941-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["老師參與人物整體發展，但還有課外來源。"],"options":["圖像只以演奏技術概括他們的發展，不包括關係與選擇。","小說否認老師對人物有任何影響。","老師參與人物整體發展，但還有課外來源。","敘述說老師已獨自決定每位樂手的人生。"]},"advanced-native-1941-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It concerns their developing character, not only the tunes they perform.","The image brings their different influences into an account of the people they grow into.","It presents identity as more than the effect of one teacher alone.","It describes the whole melody of who they become, with several experiences contributing to their developing lives."],"options":["It concerns their developing character, not only the tunes they perform.","The image brings their different influences into an account of the people they grow into.","It presents identity as more than the effect of one teacher alone.","It describes the whole melody of who they become, with several experiences contributing to their developing lives."]},"advanced-native-1941-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The whole melody of who they become refers to the students’ developing identities in this account, not merely a faster performance."],"options":["The account uses the melody only to measure how quickly they play one passage.","The critic limits the change to the music and excludes the relationships.","The whole melody of who they become refers to the students’ developing identities in this account, not merely a faster performance."]},"advanced-native-1941-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["已給出每個人的固定性格評分。"],"options":["可追問哪些經驗參與形成。","以音樂描寫人物整體發展。","已給出每個人的固定性格評分。"]},"advanced-native-1941-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The whole melody of who they become includes more than that teacher’s response; could we look at the friendships the novel also describes?"],"options":["The whole melody of who they become includes more than that teacher’s response; could we look at the friendships the novel also describes?","I thought a teacher’s early judgement was enough to explain the students’ later relationships.","I would use the performance marks alone as the summary of their characters."]},"advanced-native-1941-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The awards are part of these graduates’ stories, but not the whole melody of who they become. Read also about the care, changed interests and repaired friendships through which they describe their growth.","To hear the whole melody of who they become, we need more than the prize list. These interviews invite us to notice the choices and relationships that the graduates themselves say changed them."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1942', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1942-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["相處令說話者開始採用查來源的習慣，能力仍在發展。"],"options":["她替說話者查完所有數字，對方沒有改變做法。","說話者已不再需要練判斷來源。","這個習慣在兩人合作以前已完全相同。","相處令說話者開始採用查來源的習慣，能力仍在發展。"]},"advanced-native-1942-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["I started adopting a behaviour I had often seen her use.","The influence appeared in my own questions, not only in the reports she checked.","Her source-checking habit rubbed off on me, so I began asking where figures came from.","Repeated work together made that careful question part of my routine."],"options":["I started adopting a behaviour I had often seen her use.","The influence appeared in my own questions, not only in the reports she checked.","Her source-checking habit rubbed off on me, so I began asking where figures came from.","Repeated work together made that careful question part of my routine."]},"advanced-native-1942-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The shared habit alone does not show that it rubbed off on the earlier member from the newcomer; the timing needs to fit."],"options":["The shared habit alone does not show that it rubbed off on the earlier member from the newcomer; the timing needs to fit.","The account says the earlier member began the habit only after observing the newcomer.","Being in the same group establishes which person first influenced the other."]},"advanced-native-1942-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["對方必定刻意開課教我，並測試過我。"],"options":["可說明後來哪些做法有變化。","我受到相處中見到的習慣影響。","對方必定刻意開課教我，並測試過我。"]},"advanced-native-1942-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["A habit can rub off through working together; I started using her question without being formally taught it."],"options":["I thought an influence counted only when someone had explained the habit in a lesson.","I thought adopting her question meant my checking skills had already reached the same level as hers.","A habit can rub off through working together; I started using her question without being formally taught it."]},"advanced-native-1942-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Your patience has rubbed off on me during our film nights: I now try to hear another view before arguing for mine. Thank you for showing that a disagreement can begin with listening, even though I still need to catch myself interrupting.","The way you listen has begun to rub off on me, and I noticed it in our last discussion about the ending. I waited for the full explanation before disagreeing; I want to keep practising that rather than claim I always manage it."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
